# Alif — environment variables
# EVERY variable here is OPTIONAL. With none set, the app runs fully:
# progress is stored on the device and narration uses the browser's built-in
# Urdu/Arabic voice. Add these only to turn on the paid/cloud extras.

# --- Google Cloud Text-to-Speech (optional) ---
# Enables higher-quality cloud Urdu narration. Without it, the app falls back
# to the device's built-in speech voice. Set as a Worker secret in production.
GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY=

# --- Google Cloud Speech-to-Text (optional) ---
# Enables read-aloud mic grading on every device (records the reading and sends
# it to Google). Without it, grading falls back to the browser recognizer, which
# only works where the device has Urdu dictation. Use a SEPARATE key restricted
# to the Speech-to-Text API with a per-day quota set in Google Cloud (that quota
# is the real spend cap). If left blank, GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY is used as fallback.
# Set as a Worker secret in production.
GOOGLE_STT_API_KEY=

# --- Supabase (optional: only needed if/when accounts are added) ---
# Server-side (Worker) variables:
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=
# Client-side (baked into the browser bundle at build time):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=
